ondensed consolidated financial statements include the accounts of Xtant Medical Holdings, Inc. (“Xtant”), a Delaware corporation, and its wholly owned subsidiaries, which are jointly referred to herein as “Xtant” or the “Company”. The terms “we,” “us” and “our” also refer to Xtant. All intercompany balances and transactions have been eliminated in consolidation.","section":"Business Description and Basis of Presentation","block":96,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-036981","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-11","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001453593","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1453593/000149315226036981/form10-q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/41180c2c99b77a3f791b4e19f78f7af0834fe5515369e8f6d2d5578367cb8c77.bin","sha256":"41180c2c99b77a3f791b4e19f78f7af0834fe5515369e8f6d2d5578367cb8c77"}},{"id":"04b1d3b878b16eb3c1e5e9cca2e5ca63f8f7eb488f0495695d17be9211ca392b","quote":"The accompanying condensed consolidated balance sheet as of December 31, 2025, which has been derived from audited financial statements, and the unaudited interim condensed consolidated financial statements have been prepared in accordance with accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America (“GAAP”). They do not include all disclosures required by generally accepted accounting principles for annual consolidated financial statements, but in the opinion of management include all adjustments, consisting only of normal recurring items, necessary for a fair presentation.","context":"Xtant is a global medical technology company focused on the design, development, and commercialization of a comprehensive portfolio of orthobiologics and spinal implant fixation systems to facilitate spinal fusion in complex spine, deformity, and degenerative procedures.","section":"Business Description and Basis of Presentation","block":97,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_di